    "number": "Theorem (thm:lower_bound)",
    "quote": "Consider any $0 \\leq \\alpha^\\prime < \\alpha \\leq 1$ and $B > 0$ satisfying $T^{\\alpha} \\leq B$ and $\\lfloor T^\\alpha/2 \\rfloor \\geq \\max\\{ T^\\alpha/4, T^{\\alpha^\\prime}, 2\\}$. If an algorithm is such that $\\sup_{\\omega \\in {\\cal H}_T(\\alpha^\\prime)} R_T \\leq B$, then the regret of the same algorithm must satisfy $\\sup_{\\omega \\in {\\cal H}_T(\\alpha)} R_T \\geq 2^{-10} \\, T^{1+\\alpha} B^{-1}$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Construction uses Gaussian noise N(.,1/4) and a fixed action set of K = floor(T^alpha/2)+1 arms; can be made expressive by adding the zero action (Remark 2)."
